        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What does E10 mean on a UREVO walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              UREVO’s FAQ and its Foldi 3S manual both tie E10 to the safety lock: the pad has not detected the magnetic key for a second. Reseat or reposition the key; UREVO will send a new one if the magnet is weak or detached.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why does my UREVO walking pad keep showing E?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A flashing letter “E” on its own is UREVO’s standby symbol, according to its FAQ, and the pad can be used normally. A code with a number, such as E01 or E10, is a fault.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I tighten a UREVO walking pad belt?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Unplug the pad and turn both rear roller screws clockwise by the same amount with the hex key; UREVO’s Foldi 3S manual says 1/2 turn, then walk 1–2 minutes at 2–3 mph and repeat if needed. Do not over-tighten it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I turn off child lock on a UREVO walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              With the pad in standby, hold the speed-up button on the remote for more than 5 seconds. UREVO says you will hear a beep and the child-lock light will go off.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why does my UREVO walking pad smell like burning?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              UREVO says to lubricate under the belt, idle it for 5 to 10 minutes and let it sit for a day, then check the motor head, drive belt and fan for debris. If the smell persists, the motor may need replacing; contact UREVO.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I pair a UREVO remote?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              UREVO does not publish one pairing method for every pad. Its FAQ asks you to send the model number so it can pair the remote for that model, and it sells replacement remotes for $39.99 to $49.99.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
